---
/**
 * The project index (round 2 spec §4.2.1; R2-4; #454), Projects' lead figure: the Foundation's
 * projects as a compact list, two entries abreast (2fr : 1fr), one column below 52rem.
 *
 *   genomeOS Atlas   the name (a link to its chapter below), its status "Live, in development"
 *                    (aurora: now) and one line on what it is
 *   Next project     "More to come" (violet dashes: future), one line, and "Share an idea ↗" to
 *                    GitHub Discussions: no future project is named, because none is decided
 *
 * No mark, no button and no "Read more" (design critique of the integrated build): the Atlas
 * overview opens right below with the product itself and the one "Open the genomeOS Atlas" pill,
 * so the index only says what exists. Entry names are styled paragraphs, so "genomeOS Atlas" is
 * not a second heading beside the chapter's h2.
 */
import { GITHUB_REPOSITORY } from '../../data/nav';
---

<figure
  class="pidx"
  data-graphic="project-index"
  aria-labelledby="pidx-caption"
>
  <figcaption class="visually-hidden" id="pidx-caption">
    Our projects: the <span class="brand-name">genomeOS</span> Atlas, live and in
    development, and the next project, still to come.
  </figcaption>
  <ul class="pidx__list" data-figure-stage aria-label="Our projects">
    <li class="pidx__item pidx__item--live">
      <p class="pidx__name">
        <a href="#atlas"><span class="brand-name">genomeOS</span> Atlas</a>
      </p>
      <p class="pidx__status pidx__status--live">Live, in development</p>
      <p class="pidx__text">
        Scattered genetic data, placed and modeled on one open map.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="pidx__item pidx__item--next">
      <p class="pidx__name">Next project</p>
      <p class="pidx__status pidx__status--future">More to come</p>
      <p class="pidx__text">
        Every project starts as a community idea. <a
          class="pidx__share"
          href={`${GITHUB_REPOSITORY}/discussions`}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >Share an idea<span aria-hidden="true">&nbsp;↗</span></a
        >
      </p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</figure>
